<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:29.260
<i>It was difficult to believe that Queen Dianna would volunteer at the hospital.</i>

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:35.360
<i>Even though it was quite a struggle for her, she persisted and put herself at their service.</i>

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.950
<i>And as a result of her efforts, I have gained a beautiful memory that I'll never forget.</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:50.170
<b>Harry's Trouble</b>

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.580
Damn. It's just an empty building.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:02.100
We're sorry, please, let us go.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.270
What are they talking about!?

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.980
Nothing to see here!

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.770
That's the fifth house.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.480
This makes thirty people, so far.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.110
And there will probably be more.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.860
Another group fled last night...

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.780
I thought they were acting strangely.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.900
Hey you! What are you looking at?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.780
However, we simply can't keep them locked up like prisoners forever.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.070
Well, that is true.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.170
It's been a while since I've bumped into you here.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.460
We're having quite a hard time preventing our technicians from defecting.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.800
We're trying to keep information about this tightly regulated...

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.970
But if these escapes continue...

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.510
...the others who are returning will begin to take notice of it.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:49.100
If this situation continues, we probably won't be able to maintain our food supplies.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:53.060
We won't be able to survive with our existing rations forever.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:56.070
Do you think that food is the reason they've ran off?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.990
A man does not live on bread alone.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.490
But without bread, they also cannot live at all.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.990
As they say, you must eat in order to live.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.580
Still, this situation will only deteriorate if there are more escapees.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.870
Then, will you allow me to use any means necessary to handle this?

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:18.960
No matter how often I ask them not to fight, they continue to desire an offensive campaign.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.380
Yes. Commander Phil has said,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:27.180
he intends to damage any of the relics the Militia's excavating to be used against us.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.560
If he does so, the Militia soldiers will be forced to abandon Kingsley.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:35.270
Isn't Guin Rhineford there right now?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:42.200
Right. The Commander believes that most of the Moonrace defectors are being worked there.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.330
He intends to use that ship's destruction as an example for technicians still within Dianna Counter.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.570
That's how military officers naturally think.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.870
If Sir Guin is there, then Miss Kihel Heim must also be there.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.880
One would believe so.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.880
Are you also concerned for her?

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.090
Yes.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.700
As you too seem to be.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.970
In that case, Harry Ord, I will give you an order in the name of Dianna Soriel.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.260
Go ahead.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.770
Go to Kingsley valley, and complete the mission I've given you.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.690
But, I cannot leave you here alone at this moment!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.480
What are you saying?

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.780
This is a direct order of Dianna Soriel.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.900
Ma'am!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.490
However...

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.490
Please, return to me quickly.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.360
At this moment, you are the only person whom I'm able to trust.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.280
I understand, your majesty.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:43.870
Are you ready for it?

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.090
Go ahead.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.770
Don't try picking them up like that...

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.360
Are they usually so sharp?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.270
Is this the first time you've seen chestnuts?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.190
It almost looks like it's made of metallic needles.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.370
Milady Sochie taught me about them last year.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:17.370
So, that's the way you get at them?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.380
I'm only familiar with the ones shaped like this.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.670
Milady Kihel is very good at preparing marron glacé.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.050
Marron glacé?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.180
They're very sweet and delicious.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.790
I'd love the chance to eat it again...

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.220
Hey, are you sure I don't have to do anything else?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:38.680
- Okay, head over that way Mr. Rib!
- Can't you people do this on your own?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.190
Are those from Vicinity's Mountain Cycle?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.990
That's right. I asked our people to bring them here after uncovering them.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.570
I'm sure the White Doll could use them these days.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.710
Just what I'd expect of you, Lord heir.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.280
We're bringing the power over there.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.870
It's set to three times the output capacity.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:57.330
- What? That's too high!
- This generator's too heavy!

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.040
Lieutenant Harry, where are you going?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.090
We're currently preparing for an attack! We need all units here!

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.260
The Royal Guard should stay and help us.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.130
I am only following Queen Dianna's direct orders.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.470
An order? What are you talking about?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.610
Do you honestly expect me to tell you a Royal Guard's order?

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.890
Forget it!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.060
Stop him! Launch a WaDom!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.260
The maintenance on this WaDom isn't finished.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.270
Dammit, none of these jerks takes me seriously!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.530
Do we really have missiles now?

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:32.860
This is the first time we've tried manufacturing them ourselves. We haven't had a chance to test them yet.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:37.000
At that point, The White Doll will truly become a fighter to contend with.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.790
But the beam rifle will actually work this time, won't it?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.670
That first time, I melted it after only a few shots!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.090
You'll just have to try it anyway.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.170
That could be a problem.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.720
I understand, then.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.260
Right, a problem...

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.170
A huge problem...

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.690
Is that it?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.060
Now then, where should I try sneaking in this time?

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.060
A food storage truck?

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.780
This is going to be a very different kind of battle.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.370
Sit tight, we'll be there in just a little while.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.580
Ahh, right right, good boy...

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.090
Quite, now, please.

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.760
Alright! Stop!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.470
OK!

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.270
Ah, there we are.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.270
Hey, Mr. Horace.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:48.730
Welcome, go ahead and rest a bit.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.200
There's some food prepared for you.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.610
But for that, later tonight, I'll need you each to do some extra work.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.330
Thank you, Mister.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.490
Hey, you...

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.210
I'm glad that a young and sturdy man like yourself has joined us.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.570
l just want to try out some of the earth's fruit.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.750
I'm sorry, but I can't offer you much more than a valley full of remnants from the Dark History right now.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:12.670
As a technician, anything from the Dark History is very intriguing to me.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.790
You're also a technician? That's great to hear!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.930
Hey...Is there anyone who's currently free?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:20.180
Something wrong?

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:24.020
The shovel car seems to be in need of repairs. I'll need somebody to help take care of it.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.060
We call him Uncle Sid. Would you like to help him?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.110
You mean me?

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.570
Please! You are also of the Moonrace, right?

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.860
I'll treat you to some marron glacé later!

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.690
Uhh... sure...

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.490
How's that, Mr. Gavane?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.280
Just dandy, little lady!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:42.700
It's hard to believe a civilian house like this one will become a hospital.

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:46.290
Hmm? Why do we have to put that there?

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.880
The red cross is a sort of good luck charm.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.300
They say that the war will never spread where one of those symbols is.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.290
Really? That's bizarre.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.760
Ahh, It's coming along.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.230
Right. First, we need to detach that bolt there.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.270
It's some pretty ancient tech, isn't it?

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:10.910
More or less.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.360
And you'll also need to pound in the cylinder.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.060
Like this?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.190
If we can't get this working, we'll never get our work done.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:25.870
Is this the way things are done on earth?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.880
To someone... of the Moonrace... it might look...

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.090
it might look somewhat crude.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.840
But we sometimes need to use old tricks for old items.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.090
- I'll start hitting it again!
- Go ahead.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.850
Could this really be the place where Lady Dianna has gone off too?

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.260
Ouch...

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.560
Preparing food here isn't that easy.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:02.690
I now sympathize with our ancestors who figured out how to grow forests and agriculture on the Moon.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.290
Oho, so you've already begun the work on the ship frame?

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.290
Horace is a hard worker.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.890
That's excellent.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.090
Alright, we'll begin the next engine's tests.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.090
Move the exhaust pipe!

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.230
So, what do you think about life here on Earth?

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.560
I think I'd still like to go back to the moon.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.070
Hey, that's great!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.690
If we can get this ship to move, you can do just that!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.280
Is that possible?

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.240
It really is something else.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.280
Right now, I think I'll need to get a better generator for jump-starting the ship... but...

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.870
- What are you best at?
- I understand machines fairly well.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.290
But is this thing really a piece of technology that dates back to a forgotten part of history?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:55.840
That's correct. It's been under the protection of the nanoskin, so we're not even sure exactly how old it is.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.550
So it could be two thousand to three thousand years old?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.470
Perhaps even older.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.180
The White Doll is younger. It's sort of an exception.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.470
But it's at least 2350 years old, as well.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.590
So you believe it's older than earth's current dating system?

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:13.400
The SUMO seems to be from the same era as that mobile suit.

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.190
It appears so, but it's quite different.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:19.490
From the looks of things, their spare parts seem to be from separate eras.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:20.860
I've got it!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.660
That hurts...

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.870
Could the White Doll speed up our work by jump starting the ship's electricity?

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.780
Ahh, Good idea!

00:11:33.310 --> 00:11:36.250
Hey, do you think this beam rifle will work?

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.380
I don't know that yet.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.840
They'd like to do research on it in Nocis to see if it can be mass produced.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.470
What? That's so boring...

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.970
l want to shoot something with it!

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.560
It's not as interesting as you think it'd be.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.270
Hey! They've requested for the Mustache to go and assist the excavation.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.690
Why's that?

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.860
Lieutenant Poe, if you're about to launch, remember to use your hands to support the generator.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.380
I can handle the operation alone this time.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.090
My weapon should now be strong enough.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.080
I don't want anybody following me!

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:26.970
Excellent. Supposedly, we should be finished now.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.100
All of the engines work?

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.260
I believe so.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:38.360
I feel like I'm about to open some sort of wonderful treasure chest.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.680
Let's pray it doesn't turn out to be a Pandora's box.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.200
I'm not sure if it'll even move...

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.490
But we had our dedicated ship specialist approve this.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:49.310
The torch Will left for us is about to burn brilliantly...

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.660
Queen Dianna!

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.790
She's here, among these civilians?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.780
We're ready now!

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.630
- That won't do!
- You'll have to increase it more slowly.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:06.080
So I see... I'm moving, now.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:07.790
It's start-

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:10.350
Get down!

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:14.380
Alright, that's it! All of the engine's nozzles are lit up!

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.070
This is just like when the White Doll first moved! It's amazing!

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.190
That's exactly right.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.900
Did you see it, sister?

00:13:25.210 --> 00:13:27.110
- Let me through!
- What's your problem?

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:33.320
This shaking... If only Sir Will Game could have known...

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.370
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.120
- Madame, I need to speak with you.
- That voice is...

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.670
It's only natural to want to touch a moving object like this.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.380
That's true.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.470
You're right, it's just like what happened with the White Doll, Sochie.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:49.970
It's not quite as thrilling, but this ship's a heck of a lot bigger.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.390
That's true.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:54.270
This can't be its maximum output...

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.560
What?

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.530
Who's that?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.470
Lady Kihel is going off with that person?

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:04.360
They intend to interrupt this ship's launch?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.360
- I have been shamed. 
- Why's that?

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.870
Why was I not informed that you were here?

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.580
Don't look suspicious.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.580
This place will be targeted?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.290
- That's correct. Come with me!
- What are you doing?

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.000
I have to get you out of here at once!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.080
You only need to stop Phil's forces from attacking!

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.460
I'm here to save you because I can't possibly do that!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.090
Hey you, cut it out!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:25.710
Loran?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.470
Let go of her!

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:28.720
Don't get in my way!

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.180
This man is Lieutenant Harry.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:34.300
Harry? You're that Lieutenant from before?

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:35.970
Milady Kihel?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.900
Lady Kihel?

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.690
Lieutenant Harry has risked his life here,

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:43.570
In order to give us a warning that this valley will soon be attacked.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:46.690
Does that mean that you'll be leaving the Royal Guards and defecting to the Militia?

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.490
Don't be foolish! It's nothing of the sort!

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.570
Then have you come here to kidnap Milady Kihel?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.370
She's Queen Dianna!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.780
In this place, her name is Lady Kihel.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:03.700
Go slowly. If you're too hasty, we'll just end up crashing!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.880
- We're going slowly enough.
- Alright, go ahead.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:11.380
They may seem stupid, but those two know how to operate mechanical dolls. So they're not so bad.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:13.390
Captain! It's the "Scarecrow" mechanicals dolls.

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.890
What?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.460
Is that it?

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.230
First, I'll drag the target out by giving them a little shock.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:32.700
The gun turrets are here!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:34.030
Send the Kapools forward!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.860
Spread your bombardments to stop it from using that beam!

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.840
They came early!

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.870
Do you still believe that leaving Queen Dianna in this place would be wise?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.170
The decision to stay here is my own!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.460
Queen Dianna?

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.960
I want to stay here and live with the people of Earth.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:53.680
If you can't respect my order, I'll reveal your identity to the people working here!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.680
But Harry disguised himself Mila...

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.970
No, I mean...Your Majesty, to come and rescue you!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:01.060
If disguises are the issue, you're one to talk.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.190
I am?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.400
I'm not wearing some disguise.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.360
And what of Laura?

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.780
Well, that situation was a bit more complex...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:10.820
- Was that your hobby?
- No, just my duty.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.360
The next one's gonna hit!

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:14.780
Come with me, Laura!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.280
Will that be okay?

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.780
You have to go out in White Doll.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.370
Sister, you have to run! Loran, get the White Doll ready!

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.570
Roger!

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:28.080
It's still out of sync even after being repaired. They didn't take the refraction of an atmosphere into account.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.870
Who's Mobile Suits are those!?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.670
It won't do any good!

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.960
It won't do jack against a WaDom!

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.560
I told you we can't do anything like this!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.740
Hey, we do what we have to. We've got to earn our pay, you know?

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.470
Let's get outta here for now!

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.560
Were those things mobile suits from Dianna Counter?

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:56.480
Is Poe's upgraded WaDom the only one here?

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.500
If Mr. Horace is correct...

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.460
I can use my I-Field as a barrier...

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.990
What's that?

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.590
From the left, a beam!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.000
Oh wow!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.270
I-Field up, setting Auto Reaction to the valley!

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.090
Auto set on!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:33.060
That Mustache of theirs may be guarding the excavation site, but this beam cannon should...

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.360
Damn Militia!

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.660
Everybody, bombard it with missiles when it tries to fire that beam! Understood?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:42.870
Roger that!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.700
We'll stop it from using that Beam again!

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:49.170
The Kapool squadron's following Horace's battle strategy,

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.580
...but we won't be able to hold back their weapons with this power.

00:17:54.310 --> 00:17:57.080
What arrogance! Do you think this is enough to hold me back?

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:01.170
Let's go!

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:17.570
Is it a beam?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.860
Get down, Lady!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:19.990
Chief Horace!

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.770
It's a mega particle cannon!

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.370
The luck of the Red Cross doesn't seem to be working.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.080
Well, they still weren't hit directly, you know?

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.580
You said that the war would never shift that way!

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:40.170
In this urgent situation, I suppose I'll have to protect the enemy.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:44.670
At my feet?

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.090
Has it stopped?

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:50.690
There are two linked generators.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.800
Do we have anything that can match that output?

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.270
The Mustache stopped...

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.100
Which means there's no longer anything separating me from the spaceship!

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:58.560
In that case!

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.690
I'll finally blow it to bits with this last shot!

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.080
Lieutenant Poe, stop this!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.670
A Gold Type SUMO... Harry Ord!?

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.380
You cannot attack this valley!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.170
Did you betray us, Lieutenant Harry?

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:21.680
All of these technicians are members of the Moonrace, as well!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.460
You can't attack them!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.890
It can't be possible for him to counter this output rate!

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.080
If you intend to pass, you'll have to burn me to ashes, Poe!

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.660
Kill you? Do you wish to die as a Traitor?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:54.330
Is this the way the commander of the Royal Guard is supposed to act?

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:02.920
The Militia's backup has arrived!

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.470
Does that mean we have to help them out now?

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:09.260
No, there's no need. They've got it covered, so we'll leave.

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.970
We'd get hit without your I-Field booster, Harry. Get away from here.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:20.190
Milady Sochie is assisting the Suicide Squad with her Kapool.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.330
We should be able to fight them off...

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.480
Mustached mechanical doll...

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:29.290
Do you think you can use this?

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:31.370
What is an airship doing here?

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:34.290
There was no choice. We don't have legs like you.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:36.660
Loosen the ropes in sync with the Mustache!

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.880
We're out of line!

00:20:49.110 --> 00:20:51.670
If I aim directly for the Generator-

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.970
He's been equipped with a beam rifle?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.660
I'm aware of the Gold Type's unwillingness to fight.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.370
Please, retreat.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.160
I'll take responsibility and oversee our retreat.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.580
If you have pride as the Mustache's pilot...

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.000
...lower your gun.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.170
You still wish to return to the Dianna Counter?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.790
That's right. That Mustached mobile suit...

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:23.260
I believe that it's the White Mobile Suit of legend. The enemy of the space immigrants.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.260
You keep babbling about ancient history...

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:29.140
I'm sure it looks like one... the "Gundam", that is.

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:34.980
Ahh, is it all finished?

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:38.260
That guy's lucky to be alive.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:44.070
I'm relieved that we avoided any casualties this time.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:45.280
Yes.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:49.420
But the Hospital's tent was burned away.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:52.660
Furthermore, they've discovered our location here as well.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.160
Right.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.280
We'll have no choice but to get that thing to move.

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:02.090
Mr. Guin Rhineford will be happy about that.

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.460
That's true.

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:04.800
Sis!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.460
Good job.

00:22:12.530 --> 00:22:16.270
I personally would like to name this ship after the man who discovered it.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:20.690
I'll call it "Willgem". Still, if anyone has any other suggestions, feel free to discuss them with me.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.390
Let's do our best to complete our task and get it operational!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.290 --> 00:23:43.880
<i>Keith's bakery is doing very well for itself.</i>

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:47.000
<i>The Militia soldiers and Dianna Counter can both be called his customers.</i>

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:51.900
<i>However, at the factory Miss Teteth ends up working at, many unexpected things happen.</i>

00:23:52.820 --> 00:23:57.710
<i>And I can't help but think that the Gundam's ghost will again bring about terrible sorrow.</i>

00:23:58.650 --> 00:24:00.990
<i>Next Time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:02.960
Teteth's Last Words

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:08.380
<b>Teteth's Last Words</b>

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:05.700
"The wind shall bring tears."
